    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0865" n="753" xml:id="pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.114 Narcotics/1394: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-05T16:00:00-05:00">December 5, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Your despatch No. 77, November 6,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d758-f1"/> and
                    previous, in regard Chinese drug import permits. Please inform Chinese
                    Government that no certificate for export of narcotic drugs to China will be
                    issued except against import permit issued by Chinese Public Health
                    Administration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
